    "show_share": true,
    "description": "On Friday August 1, the Salama House, home to the Aga Khan University, Institute for Educational Development, East Africa was heaving with activity and was most definitely not 'business as usual' as it hosted the Aga Khan University's Board of Trustees. The trustees took a day out of their scheduled visit to Tanzania and spent it interacting with the students and faculty of the entities based in Dar es Salaam - the Institute for Educational Development, East Africa and the Faculty of Health Sciences (School of Nursing and Midwifery and the Medical College). This was done formally in a series of extensive discussions and continued informally over lunch.",
